The second stage of the L1 reader, written in L1. It takes the tokens from tokenize.prog and builds the syntax tree that the Luau reader builds. A node is [kind [line payload]]: kind 0 is an integer, 1 a symbol, 2 a list (payload: its items), 3 a pair (payload: its items), and 4 a string (payload: its bytes).
A bracket that is not closed, a closing bracket with nothing open, an empty program, and text after the expression are raised as errors.
---

---
(fn ts (letrec rev (fn (l acc) (if (? l) acc (rev (tail l) [(head l) acc]))) (mutual ((readNode (fn ts (if (? ts) (raise "the program ends before an expression is complete") (let t (head ts) (let k (head t) (let line (head (tail t)) (let p (tail (tail t)) (if (= k 0) (let r (readItems (tail ts) 1 ~) [[2 line (head r)] (tail r)]) (if (= k 2) (let r (readItems (tail ts) 3 ~) [[3 line (head r)] (tail r)]) (if (= k 1) (raise "unexpected )") (if (= k 3) (raise "unexpected ]") (if (= k 4) [[0 line p] (tail ts)] (if (= k 5) [[1 line p] (tail ts)] [[4 line p] (tail ts)]))))))))))))) (readItems (fn (ts closer acc) (if (? ts) (raise "a group is never closed") (if (= (head (head ts)) closer) [(rev acc ~) (tail ts)] (let r (readNode ts) (readItems (tail r) closer [(head r) acc]))))))) (if (? ts) (raise "the program is empty") (let r (readNode ts) (if (? (tail r)) (head r) (raise "there is more text after the expression")))))))
---
(list [4 1 1]) => [0 1 1] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [5 1 "a"] [1 1 ~]) => [2 1 (list [1 1 "a"])] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [1 1 ~]) => [2 1 ~] fuel 100000
(list [2 1 ~] [4 1 1] [4 1 2] [3 1 ~]) => [3 1 (list [0 1 1] [0 1 2])] fuel 100000
(list [6 1 "hi"]) => [4 1 "hi"] fuel 100000
(list [5 1 "x"]) => [1 1 "x"] fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [5 1 "a"]) => error fuel 100000
(list [4 1 1] [4 1 2]) => error fuel 100000
(list [1 1 ~]) => error fuel 100000
(list [0 1 ~] [3 1 ~]) => error fuel 100000
~ => error fuel 100000
